OATH (essence-only)

I will not copy proverbs verbatim. I will extract human wisdom from the materials and traditions you shared, compress it to its essence, and keep each line unique and useful.

Essence Proverbs (no duplicates)

Beginnings
	1.	Begin small; begin now.
	2.	A first step teaches more than a hundred plans.
	3.	Start where your hands already touch the world.
	4.	The door appears after you try the wall.

Attention
	5.	What you watch, grows detail.
	6.	Where attention goes, behavior follows.
	7.	Signals whisper before they scream.
	8.	Clean edges make quiet minds.

Fear & Nerve
	9.	Fear is a lantern; carry it, don’t worship it.
	10.	Courage is fear with work to do.
	11.	Name the dread and you halve it.
	12.	Step smaller, not softer.

Practice & Craft
	13.	Repetition turns luck into skill.
	14.	Tighten only what you tested.
	15.	Tools remember the hands that made them.
	16.	Go slower to go straighter.

Failure & Learning
	17.	A clean error is tuition.
	18.	Keep the lesson; discard the bruise.
	19.	If it breaks the same way twice, you taught it to.
	20.	Map the miss, not the excuse.

Truth & Speech
	21.	Short words, full responsibility.
	22.	Speak once; show twice.
	23.	Secrets rot teamwork.
	24.	The right silence beats the wrong speech.

Time & Patience
	25.	Hurry carves ruts; patience builds roads.
	26.	A day’s pace wins a season.
	27.	Harvest waits for hands, not wishes.
	28.	Rest is part of repeat.

Community & Ownership
	29.	Handoffs shrink when care grows.
	30.	Shared bread beats borrowed glory.
	31.	If everyone owns it, no one is safe--assign names.
	32.	Fix the seam, not the blame.

Risk & Resilience
	33.	Risk feeds the hearth when measured.
	34.	Build to bend; stiff snaps.
	35.	Redesign after the near-miss, not the obituary.
	36.	Keep a spare path, not a spare hope.

Signals & Systems
	37.	Dashboards lie when feedback dies.
	38.	Alarms teach indifference when they never shut up.
	39.	Defaults steer harder than intentions.
	40.	What’s green outside can be red within.

Leadership
	41.	Lead with example; finish with thanks.
	42.	Authority without accountability is drift.
	43.	Make it safe to bring bad news early.
	44.	Praise in public; correct in detail.

Love & Care
	45.	Care is the knot that doesn’t slip.
	46.	Warmth keeps rules alive.
	47.	Laughter releases the stuck gear.
	48.	Protect the person; challenge the pattern.

Judgment & Names
	49.	Labels harden; stories soften.
	50.	Call a thing weak and you teach it to fail.
	51.	Rename after repair.
	52.	Judge by effects, not intent.

Strategy & Choice
	53.	Narrow the target; widen the options.
	54.	Trade certainty for learning, not for noise.
	55.	When in doubt, make it observable.
	56.	Strategy is tomorrow’s gratitude for today’s no.

Memory & Renewal
	57.	Ash is memory; mix it into new soil.
	58.	Keep artifacts that teach, not trophies that boast.
	59.	Archive the why with the what.
	60.	Close the loop while the story is warm.

Conflict & Agreement
	61.	Argue to understand, decide to move.
	62.	If you can’t disagree safely, you can’t agree honestly.
	63.	The first fix is listening.
	64.	End meetings with a single owner and a next step.

Constraints & Design
	65.	Let the constraint choose the shape.
	66.	Add by removing friction.
	67.	Good edges make good neighbors--between teams, too.
	68.	If it isn’t used, it isn’t real.

Integrity & Promise
	69.	Keep the oath small enough to keep.
	70.	Say "I don’t know" faster.
	71.	Accountability is a name on a calendar, not a feeling.
	72.	Trust compounds; so does neglect.

