E1 Oath first; tools later. -- Spoken before dawn; robe "reminds" her (para 12).
E3 Fear teaches the hand before the head. -- First three breaths; bodies move, thought follows (para 6).
E5 Grip before twist. Test before trust. -- La-la’s method (paras 2, 11).
E6 Every loop is a door--check the hinge. -- Loop redirects predator; laughter oils hinge (paras 7–8).
E7 Ash is memory that warms the next fire. -- Ash rubbed for better grip (para 9).
E8 A laughing knot slips less. -- Low laughter after danger (para 8).
E9 Cracks draw the map of repairs. -- Split reed teaches where to mend (para 9).
E10 The skin decides faster than the tongue. -- Stillness taught hand-to-robe; silent cues (paras 1, 6).
E11 Practice turns luck into law. -- "Again" drill; reset and tug to song (para 11).
E12 Let obsession anchor--not drown. -- Sa-la’s held-back spark; lid closed (paras 4, 8).
E13 Care keeps the rope from cutting. -- Humane redirect, not choke (para 7).
E14 Carry a small fear like a lamp. -- Three breaths ritual; fear sized and useful (paras 6–7).
E15 When the map argues with the mud, trust the mud. -- Track reading at dawn (para 13).
E21 Skip the second look, lose the hunt. -- Roof check prevents false leak (para 10).
E23 Keep the bell honest; thresholds creep. -- Leaf on peg raises signal (para 14).

