Style Charter (reader-first)
	1.	Mythic real / concrete verbs: image comes after action.
	2.	One figure per paragraph: no purple frosting.
	3.	Aphorism earns its place: dialogue = compressed wisdom, sparingly.
	4.	Apparatus off by default: axis/seeds/totems live in endnotes.
	5.	Sensory baton: color/sound hints only when they carry plot tension.

Scene recipe (to keep "beautiful overload" under control)
	•	Beat: 7–12 sentences → 1 quiet risk → 1 repair.
	•	Checks: (a) one law implied, (b) one tool in hand, (c) one human micro-truth.
	•	Trim pass: remove any line that doesn’t move hand, heart, or hazard.

