Micro-sample (reader-mode, "Predator Night" tone)

Night pressed close. Something heavy nosed the grass. Hakaka raised a palm, and the robe learned stillness from her breath. La-la’s reed loop waited at the mouth of the shelter--quiet as a held word. Ya-la slid a pebble from her tongue to her hand; news has weight. Sa-la cupped a coal in clay, a small sun with a lid. The sound came--click, swallowed. Not panic: three breaths. Twist. Move. Reset. The thing passed. When their knees unlocked, laughter came low and true, and the loop held tighter for it.

-- AR (mini-echo): ضغط الليلُ كتفَه على العشب. لا فزع؛ ثلاثة أنفاس. لَفّ. حركة. إعادة.
-- DE (Mini-Echo): Die Nacht lehnte sich schwer auf das Gras. Kein Panikzug: drei Atemzüge. Drehen. Gehen. Neu setzen.

