Beat 9 -- Feeling as Signal (Seed-9)

[COLOR: rose red] [SFX: trembling pulse under breath]

A cold ripple ran across Hakaka’s forearms as the wind changed. Not fear-as-legend--fear-as-sensor. She raised a palm; the circle paused without shame.

Law: Treat shiver / tear / laugh as signal.

Micro-Protocol: SKIN-6 (three breaths total)
	1.	Pause one breath. (Don’t explain yet.)
	2.	Name the feeling in one word: shiver / tight / heat / tears.
	3.	Point to the body spot (skin marks the map).
	4.	Pair it to a cause guess (choose one): outside (Ω) / inside (Φ) / between (R_eff).
	5.	Act a tiny safe test (shift stance, add loop slack, swap role).
	6.	Archive with ash mark ● and one pebble if the guess proved right.

La-la’s jaw had crept tight (she hadn’t noticed). Ya-la touched her own throat--breath slice, not flow. Sa-la’s hands were too warm--spark creeping. Each named it; small fixes followed. The pulse under the scene dropped from stumble to steady thrum.

Bodily-Signals Quick Table

Code	Signal (body)	Likely Reading	Immediate Move (tiny)
S1	Shiver (skin)	environment shift (Ω↑)	add layer / rotate stance 90°
S2	Tear-prick eyes	overload/release needed	3 slow exhales; switch speaker
S3	Laugh-burst	mismatch spotted (good)	formalize as Humour-3, then fix
S4	Jaw clamp	overcontrol / pride friction	drop shoulders; ask for mirror check
S5	Shoulders up	threat rehearsal	widen feet; name the threat once
S6	Breath stutter	task too big / pace wrong	halve step; timebox one loop
S7	Cold fingers	fine work failing soon	swap roles; warm-clay 10 heartbeats
S8	Stomach knot	story risk / truth avoided	say "draft truth" in 7 words
S9	Gaze scatter	attention tax / map≻land error	touch object; describe land not plan
S10	Heat flush	spark rising (Sa-la pattern)	move ember two hand-spans; sip water

Resonance effect: good feeling-use raises A (hold) by cutting R_eff and right-sizing τ (tension) before it snaps.

⸻

Beat 10 -- Repetition as Practice (Seed-10)

[COLOR: golden loop] [SFX: triple click: tick-tick-tock]

Dawn. Three shadows in the reed light. They trained the door again, not for drama--for memory density.

Law: Once may be luck; again is life.

Protocol: DRILL-9 (quality before count)
	•	Warm (1 loop): slow-motion tie → untie → tie. [SFX: soft click]
	•	Rehearse (3 loops): run the real speed once each: La-la (grip), Ya-la (echo), Sa-la (spark).
	•	Randomize (3 loops): Hakaka calls blind cues: "L2…L5…cross-loop…smoke-veil--stop."
	•	Seal (2 loops): quiet close; check the ground; archive with ash ticks | |.

Quality Rules (no heroics):
	•	Stop on 2 misses in a row. Reset breath; slow by half.
	•	Change roles every 3 loops (prevents brittle expertise).
	•	End while clean (last loop must be your best).

Practice Schedule (Ledger card)

Cadence	Duration	What	Done mark
Daily	7 min	DRILL-9 once; rotate roles	○
2×/wk	20 min	Add noise (talk, pebble toss)	○
Weekly	45–60 min	Full scenario + SKIN-6 injects	○
Rest	1 day	Story-only replay (no loops; tell & mime)	○

Fatigue Safeguards
	•	If breath won’t smooth in 3 tries → stop.
	•	If hands go numb → swap to narrator; someone else ties.
	•	If laughter turns mean → invoke Humour-3 or end the set.

Ledger hooks: practice raises p (obsession exponent) without spiking g(Ω); variance in outcomes ↓; A climbs predictably.

