Beat 7 -- Humour Binds (Law of Laughter)

[COLOR: bright yellow] [SFX: burst chuckle → soft afterglow]

La-la misjudged the reed-door again, toe catching the second loop. The cord kissed her ankle--
[SFX: click] --and she pitched forward into Ya-la, who spilled three river pebbles like startled moons. For half a breath, shame rushed in like cold water. Then La-la’s face cracked first; Hakaka’s followed; Ya-la tried to hold sternness, failed gloriously.

Laughter arrived in the right order: pain → breath → grin → sound.
Not at the person. At the mismatch.
[SFX: hah--hah--haaah (three beats, last exhaled longer)]

Hakaka tapped the floor ash--• • •--and named the rule so their mouths could follow what their bodies already knew:

Laughter Law: A knot exhales through a laugh. We laugh at the slip, not the sister. We laugh after the check, before the fix.

They re-ran the moment on purpose: La-la reenacted the stumble in slow motion, Ya-la announced it as a story ("The Loop That Ate a Heel"), Hakaka pointed at the exact reed angle that caused the bite. Laughter thinned the sting and thickened the memory. The loop was retied a finger-width lower; the body kept the lesson even if the ash forgot.

Micro-Protocol: HUMOUR-3
	1.	Check for harm (breath steady? joint safe?).
	2.	Name the mismatch ("heel vs. height").
	3.	Laugh together (three beats), then Fix (retie, reset, replay once).

La-la brushed ash on her heel like war paint. "Again," she said, and the loop answered with neat obedience.
[SFX: click…click…(soft chuckle tail)]

Resonance effect: laughter ↓ R_eff (social resistance), dampens g(Ω) (chaos glare), so A (hold) rises without extra strain.

⸻

Beat 8 -- Crack at the Door (Catastrophe Drill)

[COLOR: black with silver fissure] [SFX: dry twig CRACK → silence → drum pickup]

Night pressed close. Something heavy nosed the grass just beyond the mouth. A dry stalk snapped--
[SFX: CRACK]. Every heart paused on the same edge.

Hakaka did not borrow heroics. She borrowed the loops.

Door Array (ASCII plan)

        OUTSIDE (night)
             ↑ river-breath
        ─────────────────────
        |   L5  o    (shoulder)   |
        |  L4  o o   (knee)       |  ← reed frame
        | L3 o   o   (ankle)      |
Entry → | L2   o o   (ankle)      |
path    |  L1 o      (heel)       |
        ─────────────────────
        INSIDE (ash circle •)

	•	L1–L3: quick-bite loops (fast, dry).
	•	L4–L5: clay-weighted loops (slower snap; signal not snare).

Roles (drilled beforehand):
	•	La-la → Shoulder Guard: drops to one knee, palm on L3 reset line; body is hinge, not wall.
	•	Ya-la → Echo-Runner: two-beat message to rear: •• (caution). Places pebble at hearth notch.
	•	Sa-la → Ember Warden: clay-wraps coal, readies smoke-veil (damp reed over ember for one lung of fog).
	•	Hakaka → Knot Caller: counts aloud the drill cadence.

DRILL: SNAP → SHIFT → SEAL (3 breaths)
	1.	SNAP -- if L1/L2 fires, nobody lunges. Hold the silence. Listen for step pattern.
[SFX: click → stillness]
	2.	SHIFT -- Hakaka calls "Two." La-la slides L3 half-span left; Ya-la ghost-moves the clay bead on L4 to slow the next bite.
[SFX: soft scratch, bead thock]
	3.	SEAL -- On "Three," Sa-la breathes the smoke-veil once across the entrance; Hakaka lays a cross-loop (over/under over both uprights) to turn rush into tangle.
[SFX: muffled whoomph…low drum]

Something tested L2. It clicked, then choked in the cross-loop. A shape backed away; the grass exhaled. The night remembered them and declined the trade.

They did not cheer. They reset slowly. Hakaka pinched ash into the mark where the visitor had trod and spoke the making-law of breaking:

Crack Law: When a loop fails in the wild, it graduates into the wall. Breakage feeds design.

Tactical Notes (for Ledger margins)
	•	Cross-Loop Tie: over-under over two uprights, kill slack before release.
	•	Clay-Bead Timing: slows snap by ~⅓ breath--buys Shift.
	•	Smoke-Veil: one lung only; second lung is retreat order.

Signal Table

Event	Beat Code	Who sends	Meaning
Quiet snap (L1–L3)	•	Loop	Hold. Listen.
Clay snap (L4–L5)	••	Ya-la	Caution; prep Shift.
Cross-loop set	•••	Hakaka	Seal; no heroics.
Retreat to ash circle	-- -- --	Any	Full fall-back, ember lift.

They practiced once more, slower, until the breath of each role matched the others. Then they slept, not braver--better braided.

