🪢 The Weave -- Poem + Equation

🌱 Poem (Seed of Birth)

The night was stone and ash.
She slid from the womb onto soil -- not cloth, not hand.
The cord hung, purple, chewed by stone.
She shivered, and the goosebumps rose like thorns.
The others thought: "Weak."
But she clawed at the air, fists closing on nothing.
Where her nails caught grass, she twisted.
A loop. A knot. A beginning.

⸻

⚖️ Ground Equation (Ledger Axis)

A = \frac{\tau \cdot (\Omega \cdot \Phi)^p}{(R_\text{eff} \cdot g(\Omega))^q}
	•	A = survival amplitude (how strong the knot holds).
	•	τ (tau) = tension, the "shiver" of fear that precedes the act.
	•	Ω (omega) = environment weight (stone, ash, soil).
	•	Φ (phi) = inner force (the claw, the twist).
	•	p = obsession power (how many times she knots again and again).
	•	R_eff = resistance from others (the "Weak" judgment).
	•	g(Ω) = distortion from chaos in the environment.
	•	q = catastrophe scaling (how harshly failure multiplies).

⸻

🪶 The Weave Explained
	•	Stone and ash → Ω (environment).
	•	Shiver → τ (tension).
	•	Claw and twist → Φ (inner force).
	•	Others thought Weak → R_eff (social resistance).
	•	Loop. Knot. Beginning. → A (survival amplitude, the new law).

Thus: the poem is the equation told in flesh and soil.
