 only)

Each idea gets one safe MVP experiment we can run in-simulation later. Nothing deploys.
1.	Quantum-entangled verification (classical first)

•	MVP: "Bell-inspired zk-commit." Use classical commitments + zk proof that a challenge/response pattern matches a CHSH-style constraint; bind to run-id & Zurich stamp.
•	Pass if: tamper-detection ≥99.9%, proof ≤1 KB, verify ≤50 ms.
•	Why now: 90% of the benefit without hardware. (Pairs cleanly with layered receipts & CANON_HASH.)  

2.	Evolutionary protocol / living genome

•	MVP: "Sandboxed mutation canary." In a sealed sim, mutate one routing rule (e.g., threshold picker), require human approval, snapshot state, auto-rollback on regression.
•	Pass if: 100% rollback success, measurable win on a pre-set objective (e.g., false-positive drop) with zero privacy regression.

3.	Incentive engine (stake/slash, privacy marketplace)

•	MVP: "Cartel pressure test." Game-theory sim with heterogeneous wealth; explore whether slashing converges to cartel power or inclusivity.
•	Pass if: cartel success <15% and Gini stays <0.6 after 1,000 rounds. (If not, park the idea.)

4.	Planetary Time (PCT)

•	MVP: "Byzantine median clock." Combine NTP, public chain headers, and a GPS trace in sim; compare to Zurich anchor.
•	Pass if: drift ≤150 ms vs Zurich across a week; failure-mode easier than Zurich-only. (Adopt only if neutrality gain > complexity.)

5.	Ambient governance (passive signals, explicit override)

•	MVP: "Opt-in synthetic cohort." Simulate usage traces; apply weekly aggregation + ε∈[0.3,0.8] DP; measure participation uplift vs re-ID risk.
•	Pass if: participation ↑ ≥8% with linkage risk ≤5% under the attacker model. (Consent + deletion flows mandatory.)

6.	Prediction-integrated policy

•	MVP: "Forecast gate on budget splits." In sim, run a tiny LMSR market predicting KPI uplift for two donation allocations; decisions only draft-gate (humans still decide).
•	Pass if: Brier score beats naive baseline by ≥15% and no single trader controls >20% influence.
 
