•	@ch_compliance: "List CH/EU flags per idea; minimal lawful paths; data-locality notes. Sign."
•	@ux: "Provide user-friendly copy for consent, receipts, and ‘how forecasts influence outcomes’. Sign."
•	@quantum: "Separate physics-real from metaphor; call out claims that must be labeled SPECULATIVE. Sign."
•	@metrics: "Define success metrics tables and telemetry needed; specify survey vs behavioral proxies. Sign."
 
Realistic timeline (three sprints)
•	Sprint 1 (Week 1): Collect all YAMLs; moderator issues scorecard + wrap.
•	Sprint 2 (Week 2): Run paper-only MVP plans (design reviews, threat maps, DP tables); no code.
•	Sprint 3 (Week 3): Decide top 1–2 experiments to simulate next (still no prod), prepare briefs for ETH Pitch & Memo lanes.
 
Risk register (what we’ll watch)
