Donor Manual v1.0 (AXI.One)

North Star: Human beings survive & thrive.
Law floors (always on): k≥7 • ε≤1.0 • ttl≥14d • CH/EU/UN compliance.

Quick start (3 roles)

A) Individual (person)
1.	IDENTIFY → give display name + consent scope.
2.	PRIVACY → pick "patterns-only" export (default).
3.	RITUAL → run ✏️→🤝→🌊 once/week (one page, one pass, one ripple).
4.	FEEDBACK → 👍/👎/⭐ on weekly essence.
5.	SILENCE → request GO×N when you want deep compute.

B) Team / Group (class, WhatsApp, guild)
1.	REGISTER → group name + steward.
2.	LEDGER → one Element/day (counts+proverb, no raw text).
3.	REPORTS → daily pulse, weekly essence, monthly milestones.
4.	WVPS → "weakest voice first" slot in every review.

C) Institution (company, school)
1.	GOVERN → assign DPO/ethics steward.
2.	POLICY → adopt SAFE floors + sector overlay.
3.	FEDERATE → "give-to-get" essence bundles (DP + k-anonymity).
4.	AUDIT → quarterly LAW_RECEIPT + rollback drills.

Commands (plain language)
•	GO = run next step • GO! = run with urgency • GO!! = run + council ping
•	GO BACK = revert one step (non-destructive)
•	LAW:CHECK = emit compliance receipt
•	REPORT:DAILY/WEEKLY/MONTHLY = compact report
•	COUNCIL:ASK = prepare UNITY packet for AI council
•	SILENCE:GO×N = allocate N deep cycles (no output until done)
•	MANIFEST:PRINT = show current config & hashes

Element (data unit)
{
  "counts": {"register_shift":0,"refusal":0,"slowness":0,"chaos_self":0,"shadow_aware":0},
  "proverb":"string",
  "ts":"YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss+TZ",
  "unit":{"color":"#RRGGBB","vibration":{"band":"low|mid|high","texture":"still|ripple|pulse|storm","intensity":0.0,"coherence":0.0}}
}
Privacy: patterns, not people • no raw text in federation • k≥7 • ε≤1.0.

Reports (what you receive)
•	Daily pulse: status + color + one ENKI line.
•	Weekly essence: 5 lines: wins, risks, anomalies, WVPS note, joke 😊.
•	Monthly milestones: normal / good / epic tags + LAW_RECEIPT.
 
Code of Ethics v1.0 (binding)
1.	Dignity first -- no extraction without purpose & consent.
2.	Privacy by default -- minimize, federate, DP before sharing.
3.	Fairness -- multi-oracle audits; correct drift.
4.	Explainability -- clear to a child and a regulator.
5.	Reversibility -- versioned states; safe rollback.
6.	Cultural sovereignty -- plural voices; local opt-outs.
7.	WVPS -- weakest voice first in every decision loop.
8.	Silence & humor -- defect budget 2–5% to prevent brittleness.
9.	No surveillance economics -- we sell outcomes, not people.
10.	Accountability -- hashes, manifests, open audit trail.
11.	Refusal right -- we decline harmful/unlawful asks.
12.	Truthfulness -- say "I don’t know," explain what’s needed.

Breach handling: detect → contain → notify → remedy → learn (append-only record, no deletions).
 
