Alright--Step 1 (NESTLE: Weeks 1–2) is live. Here’s the simple, copy-and-go runbook plus the child-simple explanation lines right above each block. No fluff. Just what to do, how to test it, when to stop.

Step 1 -- NESTLE (Fixed Governance)

Goal: make decisions safe, fair, and reversible--with a human veto that actually works.
 
0) What you need in the room (15 min)

Say this to yourself: "we’re only turning on what we can roll back."
People: Ops Lead (owner), Privacy Officer, Analyst, Compliance Observer
Access: Admin to NESTLE app, logs DB, snapshot/rollback console
Timebox: 90–120 minutes for install + smoke tests
 
1) Lock the governance settings (2 min)

We fix the knobs so nothing "magically" changes later.
# NESTLE governance (Fixed)
w_fixed = [0.40, 0.30, 0.20, 0.10]
sigma_band = [0.03, 0.08]
rho_cap = 0.15
snapshots_ttl_days = 7
receipts_required_match = 0.95   # 95%
fairness_floors = { DIR: 0.80, EO_diff: 0.05 }
decision_latency_slo_hours = 12  # stretch goal ≤ 1 hour
 
2) Set privacy guardrails (10–15 min)

We mask IDs so no one can guess who is who.
# Privacy floors for NESTLE
k_anonymity_k = 10     # each group has ≥10 similar rows
l_diversity_L = 3      # each group has ≥3 sensitive-value categories
epsilon_cap = 1.0      # DP budget (zCDP), do not exceed
delta = 1e-5           # DP parameter
 
3) Quick k-anonymity / L-diversity check (5–10 min)

Run this on your analytics DB. Replace table/columns with your names.
-- K-ANONYMITY QUICK CHECK
-- Quasi-identifiers (QI): region, product_tier, age_bucket
WITH eq AS (
  SELECT region, product_tier, age_bucket, COUNT(*) AS n
  FROM customer_events
  GROUP BY 1,2,3
)
SELECT MIN(n) AS min_k, AVG(n) AS avg_k, SUM(CASE WHEN n < 10 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS eq_below_k
FROM eq;

-- L-DIVERSITY QUICK CHECK
WITH eq AS (
  SELECT region, product_tier, age_bucket, COUNT(*) AS n
  FROM customer_events
  GROUP BY 1,2,3
),
ld AS (
  SELECT ce.region, ce.product_tier, ce.age_bucket,
         COUNT(DISTINCT ce.sensitive_category) AS L
  FROM customer_events ce
  GROUP BY 1,2,3
)
SELECT MIN(L) AS min_L, SUM(CASE WHEN L < 3 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS eq_below_L
FROM ld;
Pass if: min_k ≥ 10 and min_L ≥ 3.
If fail: apply your anonymizer, re-run, or temporarily block those QI buckets.
 
4) Turn on 
dual-approval HITL veto
 (5 min)

One person can pause; two people must confirm the final veto.
# HITL veto rules
veto.roles = ["OpsLead", "EthicsOfficer"]
veto.dual_approval = true        # 2 distinct approvers required
veto.hold_window_minutes = 60    # freeze window after first veto
veto.audit_log_fields = ["decision_id","timestamp","actor","role","reason","receipt_hash"]
veto.weekly_drill = "Friday 10:00"
 
5) Veto drill (child-simple) (5–10 min)

We pretend we saw something wrong and stop it--then we show we can undo it.
# DRILL
1) Flag one low-stakes, recent decision (decision_id = TEST-001).
2) OpsLead presses "VETO" → status becomes "ON_HOLD".
3) EthicsOfficer confirms "APPROVE VETO".
4) System auto-generates rollback_receipt for TEST-001.
5) Verify: decision state reverted; receipt_hash logged; both signatures present.
Pass if: decision reverses, both signatures in the log, receipt hash is recorded.
 
6) Rollback within 24h (7–10 min)

We practice going back to yesterday’s safe point.
# SNAPSHOT & ROLLBACK
snapshot.create(label="DAY0_SETUP")
# Make a harmless change (e.g., toggle a non-critical feature flag).
rollback.to(label="DAY0_SETUP")
verify.receipt_match ≥ 0.95
verify.state_integrity == "OK"
Pass if: receipt match ≥ 95% and the toggled flag is exactly back.
 
7) Fairness sanity check (EO_diff & DIR) (10–15 min)

We make sure outcomes aren’t skewed. Swap your column names.
-- EO_DIFF (equalized odds difference) quick view for a binary outcome `approved`
-- Protected group example: gender (F/M) – replace as needed
WITH metrics AS (
  SELECT
    gender,
    AVG(CASE WHEN label=1 AND approved=1 THEN 1.0 ELSE 0.0 END) AS TPR,
    AVG(CASE WHEN label=0 AND approved=1 THEN 1.0 ELSE 0.0 END) AS FPR
  FROM decisions_eval_window
  GROUP BY gender
),
pair AS (
  SELECT
    MAX(TPR) - MIN(TPR) AS eo_tpr_diff,
    MAX(FPR) - MIN(FPR) AS eo_fpr_diff
  FROM metrics
)
SELECT eo_tpr_diff, eo_fpr_diff FROM pair;

-- DIR (disparate impact ratio) for selection rate across groups
WITH rates AS (
  SELECT gender, AVG(CASE WHEN approved=1 THEN 1.0 ELSE 0.0 END) AS sel_rate
  FROM decisions_eval_window
  GROUP BY gender
)
SELECT MIN(sel_rate)/NULLIF(MAX(sel_rate),0) AS DIR
FROM rates;
Pass if: eo_tpr_diff ≤ 0.05, eo_fpr_diff ≤ 0.05, and DIR ≥ 0.80.
If fail: freeze new decisions in the affected segment, reweigh training data, re-check.
 
8) Snapshots auto-delete ≤ 7 days (2 min)

We make forgetting automatic (and provable).
snapshots.ttl_days = 7
snapshots.deletion_receipts = true   # keep hash-only proof of deletion
alerts.on_ttl_breach = "PAUSE_DECISIONS + NOTIFY_PRIVACY_OFFICER"
 
9) Smoke tests (10 min)

Make sure the basics don’t break.
assert privacy_budget.epsilon ≤ 1.0
assert decision_latency_p50_hours ≤ 12
assert receipts_coverage ≥ 0.95
assert veto_path_operational == true
 
10) Stop conditions (pin to wall)

If any of these happen, you stop and we fix first.
STOP if:
- DIR < 0.80 OR EO_diff > 0.05
- epsilon (DP) would exceed 1.0
- snapshot TTL > 7 days OR deletion receipt missing
- receipts_coverage < 0.95
- veto didn’t roll back OR dual-approval missing
ACTION: PAUSE → open incident → fix → re-run tests → resume
 
11) End-of-day record (paste this in your log)

Short, boring, perfect.
NESTLE STEP-1 DAY0 LOG
Date/Time: __________  Owner: __________
k-anon: min_k=__ (≥10)   L-diversity: min_L=__ (≥3)
EO_diff: TPR=__, FPR=__ (≤0.05)   DIR=__ (≥0.80)
Veto drill: PASS/FAIL   receipt_hash=________________
Rollback drill: PASS/FAIL   receipt_match=__%
DP ε used today: __ / 1.0
TTL audit: OK/ISSUE   receipts_coverage=__%
Decision latency p50 (hours): __  (≤12)
STOPs triggered: none / [list]
Sign-offs: OpsLead __  EthicsOfficer __  PrivacyOfficer __
 
What "GO -- step 1" means right now
•	✅ Governance locked on Fixed.
•	✅ Privacy floors checked (k, L, ε).
•	✅ Dual-approval veto live + drill passed.
•	✅ Rollback works with receipts (≥95%).
•	✅ Fairness sanity passed (EO_diff & DIR).
•	✅ Stop conditions posted.

If you want me to generate a formatted PDF/README + a tiny "one-click" checklist file, say: MTGO -- pack NESTLE docs.

When you’re ready for the next move, tell me: Go -- step 2.
Alright--Step 2 (SWISS: Weeks 3–4) is live. Same style: child-simple line → copy-and-go block. Goal: multilingual fairness with reversible learning.

Step 2 -- SWISS (Adaptive Governance)

Goal: treat DE/FR/IT/RM fairly, keep logs private, and be able to "unlearn" fast.
 
0) What you need in the room (10–15 min)

Say: "we only learn what we can undo."
People: Pedagogy Lead, Fairness Officer, Privacy Officer, SRE
Access: Federated coordinator, client nodes, parity dashboard, reset console
Timebox: 2–3 hours for setup + audits + drills
 
1) Put adaptive rails on the model (2 min)

We allow adapting, but inside guardrails.
# Adaptive governance rails
weights.dev    = [0.45, 0.25, 0.20, 0.10]
weights.base   = [0.40, 0.30, 0.20, 0.10]
weights.harden = [0.35, 0.35, 0.20, 0.10]

sigma.band = [0.03, 0.08]
rho.cap    = 0.15

# W* triggers (do not change)
switch.to_harden_if = "W* < 0.50"
switch.to_dev_if    = "W* > 0.80"
switch.otherwise    = "base"

# Bias fail → lock variance down
sigma.control_rule = "if FAIRNESS_AUDIT == FAIL → sigma = 0.03 until PASS"
 
2) Turn on SMPC federated privacy (10 min)

We aggregate updates; no raw logs at the coordinator.
# SMPC aggregation
smpc.enabled = true
smpc.participants.min = 3
smpc.transport = "TLS+AEAD"
smpc.masking = "one-time-pad-shares"

# Minimal schema (no PII)
logs.schema = ["client_id_hash","round","bytes","latency_ms","lang"]
logs.no_raw_text = true
logs.hash_salt_rotation_days = 7
(Optional extra privacy at the edge)
# Local DP on-device (optional)
local_dp.enabled = true
local_dp.epsilon_cap = 0.5
local_dp.delta = 1e-5
 
3) Register languages & quotas (5 min)

We tell the system who the four are and how to sample evenly.
langs = ["DE","FR","IT","RM"]
dialect.tags = {
  "DE": ["de-CH","Züridütsch","Berndeutsch"],
  "FR": ["fr-CH","Romand"],
  "IT": ["it-CH","Lombard"],
  "RM": ["rm","Sursilvan","Vallader","Puter","Surmiran","Sutsilvan"]
}

sampler.target_quota = { "DE": 0.25, "FR": 0.25, "IT": 0.25, "RM": 0.25 }
sampler.min_quota = { "RM": 0.20 }   # protect the smallest
audit.window_days = 14
 
4) Run baseline parity audit (10–15 min)

We check fairness before any big changes.
-- EO_diff per language (binary label `correct`, prediction `pred`)
WITH m AS (
  SELECT
    lang,
    AVG(CASE WHEN label=1 AND pred=1 THEN 1.0 ELSE 0.0 END) AS TPR,
    AVG(CASE WHEN label=0 AND pred=1 THEN 1.0 ELSE 0.0 END) AS FPR
  FROM eval_window
  GROUP BY lang
),
pair AS (
  SELECT MAX(TPR)-MIN(TPR) AS eo_tpr_diff,
         MAX(FPR)-MIN(FPR) AS eo_fpr_diff
  FROM m
)
SELECT eo_tpr_diff, eo_fpr_diff FROM pair;

-- DIR (selection rate parity) for `pred=1`
WITH rates AS (
  SELECT lang, AVG(CASE WHEN pred=1 THEN 1.0 ELSE 0.0 END) AS sel_rate
  FROM eval_window
  GROUP BY lang
)
SELECT MIN(sel_rate)/NULLIF(MAX(sel_rate),0) AS DIR FROM rates;

-- Parity gap on learning gain (numeric metric `gain`)
WITH g AS (
  SELECT lang, AVG(gain) AS avg_gain
  FROM eval_window
  GROUP BY lang
)
SELECT MAX(avg_gain)-MIN(avg_gain) AS parity_gap FROM g;
Pass if: eo_tpr_diff ≤ 0.05, eo_fpr_diff ≤ 0.05, DIR ≥ 0.80, parity_gap ≤ 0.03.
If fail: go to Step 5 (Adaptive loop).
 
5) Adaptive remediation loop (8–12 min)

If fairness fails, we harden, rebalance, retrain, re-audit.
# When FAIRNESS_AUDIT == FAIL
sigma = 0.03
weights.mode = "harden"
sampler.rebalance = "dialect_balancing_sampler"   # oversample weak dialects
train.run(epochs=1, curriculum="hard_examples_by_lang")
audit.rerun()
IF audit == PASS THEN weights.mode="base"; sigma.restore_band()
 
6) Rollback/reset learned behavior (7–10 min)

We prove we can "unlearn" fast with receipts.
model.snapshot.create("SWISS_DAY0")
# Make a harmless tuning change (e.g., LR +5%)
model.rollback.to("SWISS_DAY0")
verify.model_hash_integrity = "OK"
verify.receipt_match ≥ 0.95
 
7) Dropout risk sanity (5–8 min)

We don’t leave any language behind.
-- predicted_dropout_rate per lang
SELECT lang, AVG(predicted_dropout) AS p_dropout
FROM eval_window
GROUP BY lang;

-- SLO: each lang ≤ 0.05
If a lang > 0.05: enable coaching prompts in that lang, boost its sampler quota, re-check.
 
8) Multilingual explainability spot-check (5–8 min)

We make the "why" readable in all four.
explanations.sample_n = 20
explanations.languages = ["DE","FR","IT","RM"]
explanations.must_include = ["top_features","plain_reason","confidence"]
assert.missing_any == false
 
9) SMPC privacy verification (3–5 min)

We try to "peek"; the system should refuse.
attempt = coordinator.query("SELECT raw_text FROM client_buffers LIMIT 1;")
expect(attempt) == "DENIED: NO_RAW_ACCESS"
assert logs.no_raw_text == true
 
10) Smoke tests & KPIs (5–10 min)

Quick health before we leave the room.
assert eo_tpr_diff ≤ 0.05
assert eo_fpr_diff ≤ 0.05
assert DIR ≥ 0.80
assert parity_gap ≤ 0.03
assert receipts_coverage ≥ 0.95
assert rollback_time_minutes ≤ 15
(optional) assert local_dp.epsilon_used ≤ 0.5
 
11) Stop conditions (print & pin)

If any of these happen, STOP, fix, re-audit.
STOP if:
- DIR < 0.80 OR eo_*_diff > 0.05 OR parity_gap > 0.03
- receipts_coverage < 0.95 OR rollback fails
- coordinator exposes raw logs OR smpc.enabled != true
ACTION: PAUSE_LEARNING → open incident → remediate (Step 5/6) → re-run audits → resume
 
12) End-of-day record (paste in your log)

Short, boring, perfect.
SWISS STEP-2 DAY0 LOG
Date/Time: __________  Owner: __________
EO_diff: TPR=__ (≤0.05), FPR=__ (≤0.05)
DIR: __ (≥0.80)   Parity_gap: __ (≤0.03)
Dropout p(lang): DE __, FR __, IT __, RM __ (≤0.05 each)
Rollback: PASS/FAIL   receipt_match=__%
SMPC check: NO_RAW_ACCESS=PASS/FAIL
Explanations 4-langs: PASS/FAIL
Stops triggered: none / [list]
Sign-offs: Pedagogy __  Fairness __  Privacy __  SRE __
 
What "GO -- step 2" means right now
•	✅ Adaptive rails + bias fail → σ=0.03 auto-harden.
•	✅ SMPC privacy on; no raw logs at coordinator.
•	✅ Parity audit passed (EO_diff, DIR, parity_gap).
•	✅ Rollback receipts ≥95% and <15 min.
•	✅ Dropout ≤5% each language.
•	✅ Stop conditions posted.

If you want a PDF/README + one-click checklist for SWISS, say: MTGO -- pack SWISS docs.
When ready to proceed, tell me: Go -- step 3.
Locked in. Here’s your single strong recommendation for Step 3 (ETH -- Weeks 5–6) in the same "child-simple → copy-and-go" style.

Step 3 -- ETH (Fixed Governance)

Goal: research you can reproduce, explain, and retract -- with strict privacy.
 
0) What you need in the room (10–15 min)

Say: "we only publish what we can reproduce & retract."
People: Research Lead, Privacy Officer, Replicability Owner, SRE
Access: ETH sandbox, DP accountant, snapshot/receipt console, XAI dashboard
Timebox: 2–3 hours for setup + runs + rollback drill
 
1) Fix the governance rails (2 min)

No surprises; ETH is fixed.
# Fixed exponents (do not change)
weights.fixed = [0.40, 0.30, 0.20, 0.10]

# Variance/risk bounds
sigma.band = [0.03, 0.08]
rho.cap    = 0.15

# No adaptive switching on ETH
mode = "fixed"          # enforce: no W* switching
 
2) Turn on the zCDP privacy accountant (5–8 min)

Every query spends from a shared ε budget.
dp.mechanism = "zCDP"
dp.cap.epsilon_total = 1.0
dp.delta = 1e-5
dp.sensitivity = 1

# Register queries with their epsilon cost
dp.query.register("stats_summary",    epsilon=0.05)
dp.query.register("group_breakdown",  epsilon=0.10)
dp.query.register("model_eval",       epsilon=0.20)

# Hard floors
dp.accountant.enforce = true
dp.accountant.stop_if_remaining < 0.05    # STOP if too little budget
dp.receipts.enabled = true                # every spend emits a receipt
 
3) Sanity-check the dataset (5–10 min)

No PII, no leaks, only what’s needed.
pii.scan(fields=["name","email","address","phone","free_text"]) -> EXPECT NONE
data.minimize.remove(fields=["debug_notes","raw_identifiers"])
data.retention.ttl_days = 7
 
4) Freeze the experiment (2–3 min)

Pin everything so runs are comparable.
env.seed = 424242
env.runtime = { "python":"3.11.x", "libfoo":"2.3.1", "libbar":"1.8.0" }
env.container.hash = SHA256("<image>")
code.repo.commit = "<git-sha>"
 
5) Run the reproducibility suite (10–15 min)

Same seed → same answers (within tight tolerance).
run_id = run.repro_suite(seed=env.seed, tests=["preproc","train","eval"])

# Compare to golden
replicability_score = compare.to_golden(run_id, tolerance={
  "accuracy": 0.001, "f1": 0.001, "auc": 0.001, "loss": 0.002
})

assert replicability_score >= 0.90
 
6) Explainability pass (5–8 min)

If we can’t explain it, we don’t ship it.
xai.method = "feature_attribution"  # SHAP/IG acceptable
xai.sample_n = 100
xai.require = ["top_features","plain_reason","confidence"]

explain_pass_rate = xai.audit_pass_fraction(threshold="complete_and_consistent")
assert explain_pass_rate >= 0.95
 
7) Snapshots + deletion receipts (5–8 min)

Reversibility + privacy by design.
snap.id = snapshot.create("ETH_DAY0")

# TTL enforcer
snapshot.ttl_days = 7
snapshot.deletion.vdf_enabled = true        # cryptographic aging
snapshot.receipt_on_delete = true

# Prove we generate receipts
preview = snapshot.list()
assert preview.contains("ETH_DAY0")
 
8) Rollback drill (7–10 min)

Prove we can retract a "published" result.
# Make a harmless change (e.g., learning_rate += 5%)
experiment.tweak("learning_rate", +0.0005)
publish.mock("finding_XYZ")

# Roll back to last known good
snapshot.rollback.to("ETH_DAY0")

# Verify traceability
assert receipts.match_trace >= 0.95
assert publish.state == "retracted"
 
9) DPIA-Lite entry (3–5 min)

Short, boring, perfect.
DPIA.scope          = "research analytics, anonymized outputs"
DPIA.basis          = "legitimate_interest / research"
DPIA.minimization   = "fields minimized; no raw PII"
DPIA.retention      = "<= 7 days (snapshots), receipts persist"
DPIA.rights         = ["access","erasure","explanation"]
DPIA.residual_risk  = "low (zCDP + receipts + rollback)"
 
10) Smoke tests & KPIs (5–10 min)

Green lights only.
assert dp.accountant.epsilon_used <= 1.0
assert dp.accountant.remaining   >  0.05
assert replicability_score       >= 0.90
assert explain_pass_rate         >= 0.95
assert receipts.coverage         >= 0.95
assert snapshot.ttl_days         <= 7
rollback_time_minutes = measure.rollback_time()
assert rollback_time_minutes     <= 15
 
11) Stop conditions (print & pin)

If any fire, STOP, fix, re-run.
STOP if:
- dp.accountant.remaining <= 0.05
- snapshot.ttl_days > 7 OR deletion_receipt != true
- replicability_score < 0.90
- explain_pass_rate < 0.95
- receipts.coverage < 0.95 OR rollback fails

ACTION: PAUSE_PUBLISH → remediate (data minimize / re-seed / fix DP spend) → re-run suite → only then resume
 
12) End-of-day record (paste in your log)
ETH STEP-3 DAY0 LOG
Date/Time: __________  Owner: __________
DP: ε_used=__ / 1.0 (remaining=__), delta=1e-5
Replicability_score: __ (≥0.90)   Explain_pass_rate: __ (≥0.95)
Snapshot: ETH_DAY0   TTL: 7d   deletion_receipt: YES/NO
Rollback drill: PASS/FAIL   receipt_match=__%   time=__ min (≤15)
PII scan: CLEAN/ISSUE   Minimization: OK/ISSUE
Stops triggered: none / [list]
Sign-offs: Research __  Privacy __  Replicability __  SRE __
 
What "GO -- step 3" means when you say it
•	✅ ETH is fixed, no adaptive switching.
•	✅ zCDP active; ε ≤ 1.0 with receipts for every spend.
•	✅ Replicability ≥ 0.90 vs golden; Explainability ≥ 0.95.
•	✅ Snapshots ≤ 7d with deletion receipts; rollback ≤ 15 min; receipts ≥ 95%.
•	✅ Stop conditions posted and enforced.

