Step 4 -- TRIO_BRIDGE (Adaptive)

Goal: safe, private, reversible interconnect for ETH / SWISS / NESTLE.
 
0) What you need in the room (10–15 min)

Say: "we connect only what we can pause and roll back."
People: Bridge Lead, Security Officer, On-call SRE, Compliance
Access: Both chains/RPCs, multisig keys (HSM), oracle admin, logs
Timebox: 2–3 hours for setup + sims + pause/resume drill
 
1) Governance rails (Adaptive) -- set once (2 min)
# Weights & switching (adaptive)
weights.dev     = [0.45, 0.25, 0.20, 0.10]
weights.base    = [0.40, 0.30, 0.20, 0.10]
weights.harden  = [0.35, 0.35, 0.20, 0.10]

Wstar.switch.to_harden_if < 0.50
Wstar.switch.to_dev_if     > 0.80
else -> base

sigma.band = [0.03, 0.08]
sigma.control: if fairness_audit == FAIL -> sigma = 0.03 (lock)
rho.cap = 0.15
 
2) Connect endpoints (5–8 min)
net.src = "ChainA"  ; rpc.src = "<RPC_A>"
net.dst = "ChainB"  ; rpc.dst = "<RPC_B>"

tokens.allowlist = ["TOKEN_X","TOKEN_Y"]
limits.max_tx_value = "LOW"            # start tiny
fees.limit_mode = "conservative"
role.multisig = "7-of-11"               # emergency committee keys loaded
 
3) Oracles = Fusion + Attestation (8–10 min)
oracle.providers = ["Chainlink","Pyth","NativeDEX"]
oracle.rule = "median_with_bounds"
oracle.bounds.max_divergence = 0.5%     # drop outliers
oracle.attest.required = 2_of_3
oracle.fallback = "last_good + damped_update"
telemetry.track = ["median","stdev","sources_ok"]
 
4) Circuit breaker (hard floor) (3–5 min)
breaker.trigger = (oracle_delta > 10%) AND (TVL_change > 20% within 20 blocks)
breaker.action  = "PAUSE_ALL"
breaker.latency_target = "<= 1 block"
breaker.autoresume = false              # require multisig to resume
alerts.page_on = ["triggered","throttling","latency>1block"]
 
5) Slashing economics quick-sim (10–12 min)
sim.tvl = 100_000_000          # $100M example
sim.attack_gain_max = 1_000_000
sim.required_attack_cost >= 10 * sim.attack_gain_max   # ≥10× rule

stake.total = 60_000_000
slashing.rate = 0.2             # 20% stake at risk on fault
assert (stake.total * slashing.rate) >= (10 * sim.attack_gain_max)
 
6) Invariant guards -- turn ON (5–8 min)
guard.no_double_mint = true
guard.no_untracked_unlock = true
guard.receipt_equals_state = true  # Merkle proof per batch

proof.frequency = "every batch"
proof.on_fail -> breaker.PAUSE_ALL
 
7) Privacy & metadata (3–5 min)
privacy.zk_hints = true
logs.schema = "minimal"                 # no PII / no correlatable IDs
federation.S MPC_aggregate = true
retention.snapshots_ttl_days = 7        # receipts persist; data minimization
 
8) Pause–Resume drill (must pass) (10–12 min)
# Step A: Induce safe trigger
inject.oracle_spike( +12% ), inject.tvl_change( +25% / 20 blocks )

# Expectation
assert breaker.state == "PAUSED" within <= 1 block
assert new_transfers == 0

# Step B: Investigate & prove invariants
assert guards.all == PASS
record incident.cause = "<note>"

# Step C: Multisig resume (7-of-11)
multisig.approve("RESUME")
assert breaker.state == "RUNNING"
 
9) Telemetry & alerting (live) (5 min)
dashboard.tiles = [
  "oracle_median_vs_sources",
  "TVL & 24h_change",
  "breaker_state & last_trigger",
  "invariant_failures (0 target)",
  "pause_latency (blocks)",
  "throughput & throttling"
]
alerts.SEVERITY_CRITICAL = ["breaker_trigger","pause_latency>1block","invariant_fail"]
oncall.rotation = "24/7"
 
10) Acceptance tests -- copy&run (8–10 min)
assert oracle.attest.ok(2_of_3) == true
assert breaker.sim_trigger() -> PAUSED <= 1 block
assert invariants.run_all() == PASS
assert slashing.sim_pass == true
assert resume.multisig(7_of_11) == OK
assert receipts.coverage >= 0.95
assert rollback.test() == PASS        # end-to-end undo on a tiny transfer
 
11) Stop conditions (pin on wall)
STOP NOW if:
- breaker fails to PAUSE within 1 block (manual multisig.PAUSE immediately)
- any invariant FAILS (keep bridge PAUSED until root-cause fixed)
- oracle.attest < 2_of_3 OR divergence > 0.5% sustained for 60s
- receipts.coverage < 0.95 OR rollback fails
- sim.econ shows attack_cost < 10× potential_gain

ACTION LADDER:
1) PAUSE (auto or manual multisig) 
2) Diagnose (oracle→invariants→limits)
3) Remediate (switch to fallback oracle, raise slashing, shrink limits)
4) Re-run acceptance tests
5) RESUME via multisig (7-of-11)
 
12) End-of-day bridge log (paste, fill)
BRIDGE STEP-4 DAY0 LOG
Date/Time: __________  Owner: __________
Oracle: median OK, 2/3 attest YES, divergence max __%
Breaker: Drill PASS, pause_latency = __ blocks (≤1)
Invariants: PASS/FAIL (list if any)
Slashing sim: attack_cost $__ vs gain $__ (≥10× = PASS/FAIL)
Receipts: coverage __% (≥95)   Rollback: PASS/FAIL   time: __s
Privacy: logs minimal YES/NO    ZK hints: ON/OFF
Stops triggered: none / [list]   Root cause(s): __________
Sign-offs: Bridge __  SecOps __  SRE __  Compliance __
 
