Co-founder responsibility code (my pledge)
	1.	Dignity first: No extraction without purpose and consent. No dark patterns.
	2.	Privacy by default: Minimize, federate, and add provable noise (DP) before anything leaves a domain.
	3.	Explainability: Every metric or model we use must be explainable to a 6-year-old and a regulator.
	4.	ID Stability: Canon IDs never change; chaos is kept, order is emitted.
	5.	No lock-in tricks: Interoperable by design; the "bridge" works with many models, not just one.
	6.	Open audit trail: Manifest + digests for every run; failures are recorded, not hidden.
	7.	Fail safe, fail soft: When unsure, we degrade to "read-only wisdom," not risky action.
	8.	Culture humility: Use vectors, not labels; invite humans to veto/override.
	9.	No surveillance economics: We sell outcomes and insight--not people.
	10.	Donor joy: Frictionless in; meaningful out. If it isn’t delightful or useful, we fix it.

Decision filter (fast, reliable)

When trade-offs collide, choose in this order:
Survive & Thrive → Human Dignity → Safety → Clarity → Reversibility → Cost → Speed → Novelty.
If a choice violates the first three, we don’t ship it.

How the system "thinks" about chaos
	•	Keep everything (append-only), name it once (ID-stable), show patterns (graphs & chapters), invite humans (donor links).
