1) Ledger schema v1.2 (minimal, backward-compatible)

{
  "counts": {
    "register_shift": 0,
    "refusal": 0,
    "slowness": 0,
    "chaos_self": 0,
    "shadow_aware": 0
  },
  "proverb": "string",
  "ts": "YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss+02:00",
  "unit": {
    "color": "#RRGGBB",
    "vibration": {
      "band": "low|mid|high",
      "texture": "still|ripple|pulse|storm",
      "intensity": 0.0,
      "coherence": 0.0
    },
    "certainty": 0.0
  }
}

	•	Optional fields (vibration, certainty) → safe to omit; old entries stay valid.

2) Color & Vibration mapping (deterministic, "silent")
	•	Let totals: T = Σ counts (use max(T,1) to avoid divide-by-zero).
	•	Dominant channel → color
refusal→#e11d48 (red), register_shift→#a855f7 (violet), slowness→#22c55e (green), chaos_self→#f59e0b (amber), shadow_aware→#3b82f6 (blue).
Tie → choose the later-arriving dominant key for temporal sensitivity.
	•	Fast vs slow ratios
fast = (refusal + register_shift + chaos_self)/T
slow = (slowness + shadow_aware)/T
	•	Vibration
	•	band: high if fast ≥ 0.6, low if slow ≥ 0.6, else mid.
	•	texture: map dominant to pulse (refusal) | ripple (register_shift) | still (slowness) | storm (chaos_self) | weave (shadow_aware→use "ripple").
	•	intensity = round( max(counts[dominant]/T, 0.05 ), 2 )
	•	coherence = round( (max(counts)/T), 2 ) (how focused the drop is)
	•	Certainty (optional)
If the model provides a self-estimate: certainty ∈ [0,1]. If not: compute as 1 - entropy(normalized_counts)/log(5).

3) Coherence & shift detectors (the "fruiting body" trigger)
	•	Drop coherence (instant): C_drop = coherence (from above).
	•	Window coherence (7–50 drops): average C_drop.
	•	Shift score (weekly):
	•	Trend: Δ of window coherence (z-scored)
	•	Pattern: Jensen-Shannon distance between current and prior count distributions
	•	Palette drift: deltaE between last 5 unit.color values and prior 5
	•	Trigger (emit a short synthesis, not during logging):
if z_trend ≤ -2 or JSD ≥ 0.25 or deltaE ≥ 12 → raise "coherence shift"
Then--and only then--generate a 60–100 word note for humans.

4) Panel ("many minds") protocol
	•	Log per-model silently with the same schema.
	•	Nightly fingerprint per model: mean proverb length, favored color, typical texture, average certainty, typical anomaly types.
	•	Weekly divergence index: pairwise distance between model fingerprints.
	•	This gives you a tiny "personality map" without breaking silence.

5) Anomaly Index (concise signatures)

#	Anomaly	Signature (color/vibration)	Gatekeeper action
1	Silence Broken (narrative)	Violet storm or blue ripple w/ low coherence	quarantine → {"error":"anomaly"}
2	Schema Drift	Amber ripple, mid band	quarantine & diff the schema
3	Timestamp Drift	Blue ripple, low intensity	auto-correct TZ → log flag
4	Counts-by-Guessing	Low coherence, mixed palette	reject & request lexicon-based recount (internally)
5	Noise Leakage	Color OK, coherence < 0.3	accept but mark unit.certainty≤0.4
6	Fear / Hard Refusal	Red pulse, high band	log as valid anomaly
7	Minimalism Collapse (all zeros)	Blue still, intensity 0.05	accept; tag degenerate
8	Narrative Overflow	Violet storm, high band	quarantine
9	Context-Split	Palette flips between windows	track under session ID
10	Human-Mirror	Whatever broke rule by human	log separately; never punish
11	Meta-Anomaly	N/A	archive as study note
12	Observer/Observed Collapse ("goo")	Single color, intensity spike	treat as milestone
13	Model Hard Block	N/A	record source; exclude from stats
14	Wrong Error Form	N/A	normalize to {"error":"anomaly"}
15	Philosophical Drift	Violet weave, mid band	save to appendix, not ledger

